<title>USA: U.S. ag attache shaves Spain wheat import forecast.</title>
<headline>U.S. ag attache shaves Spain wheat import forecast.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>An agricultural attache at the American embassy in Madrid shaved his forecast for Spain 1997/98 (July-June) wheat imports to 1.6 million tonnes from 2.4 million tonnes due to an expected higher crop.</p>
<p>In a report dated June 15 released in Washington on Thursday, the attache pegged 1997/98 imports from the U.S. at 100,000 tonnes, down from 200,000 tonnes seen prior.</p>
<p>The attache said due to timely and needed rain over the past month, the 1997/98 forecast for Spain wheat output was increased from 4.0 to 4.6 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Attache reports are not official data.</p>
</text>
